{"frame":"event","cursor":101,"box":"cf-missing-tool-3-57832","box_id":3,"session":3,"kind":"agent_said","payload":{"text":"I ran shellcheck 0.10.0 on the four shell scripts under `scripts/`. It found one issue, and I left the scripts unchanged. `scripts/ios-app-drawn.py` is Python, so I didn't lint it.\n\n**Clean:** `check-android.sh`, `check-ios.sh` and `check-stack.sh`.\n\n**`scripts/moor-setup.sh:122`, SC2086 (info level):**\n```sh\nif [ \"$#\" -eq 0 ] || [ \"$1\" = all ]; then set -- $all; fi\n```\n`$all` is unquoted, so it is word-split and glob-expanded.\n\nI wouldn't apply shellcheck's suggested fix of `set -- \"$all\"`. The unquoted split looks deliberate, because it turns a space-separated list of names into separate positional arguments. Quoting it would collapse them into one argument and break the \"all\" case.\n\nIf the names never contain spaces or glob characters, the code is fine as it is. To silence the warning, add `# shellcheck disable=SC2086` above the line. If you want it stricter, switch `$all` to an array."},"ts":1795757861980}
